  "companyName": "Corsair Gaming, Inc.",
  "country": "US",
  "debtToEquityTTM": null,
  "description": "Corsair Gaming, Inc., operating with its subsidiaries, specializes in the development, promotion, and global distribution of high-performance hardware and software for the gaming and live-streaming communities. Its extensive reach covers the Americas, Europe, the Middle East, and the Asia Pacific region. The company's product lineup features a broad range of peripherals for gamers and content creators, including specialized keyboards, precision mice, immersive headsets, and versatile controllers. For streamers, it offers essential tools such as video capture devices, customizable stream decks, professional USB microphones, studio accessories, and the EpocCam software. Furthermore, Corsair supplies critical PC components and complete system solutions, encompassing power supply units, advanced cooling systems, diverse computer cases, and high-speed DRAM modules. This also extends to providing both pre-assembled and custom-built gaming PCs. Complementing its hardware, the company develops proprietary software like iCUE for optimizing gaming experiences and Elgato's integrated suite for streamers and content creators. Beyond products, Corsair delivers additional services, including coaching and training. Its sales strategy leverages a wide network of distributors and retailers, including major online platforms, in addition to direct sales to consumers via its own corporate website. Incorporated in 1994, Corsair Gaming, Inc. is headquartered in Fremont, California, and functions as a subsidiary of Corsair Group (Cayman), LP.",
